1) Check the C++, AN) TLR, CMake, Boost and Qt versions\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 a) Clang, C++14 at least\
b) CMake version >= 3.12\
c) Boost version >= 1.71\
d) Qt version >= 6\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 2) For Linux, select the Clang compiler\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 a) set CC=clang\
b) set CXX=clang++\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 3) Create a directory to hold the source projects\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 a) mkdir git.repositories\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 4) Create the destination directory\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 a) sudo mkdir /opt\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 5) Clone the mdns_plusplus repository and build it\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 a) cd ~/git.repositories\
b) git clone https://opendragon@github.com/opendragon/mdns_plusplus.git\
c) cd mdns_plusplus/non-iOS\
d) git pull\
e) ccmake .\
f)\'a0 Set the CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE to Release\
g) Set the CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX to '/opt/mdns_plusplus' or 'C:/Program Files/mdns_plusplus' if for Windows\
h) Configure and generate\
i) cmake .\
j) make\
k) sudo make install\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 6) Clone the ODL repository and build it\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 a) cd ~/git.repositories\
b) git clone https://opendragon@github.com/opendragon/ODL.git\
c) cd ODL/non-iOS\
d) git pull\
e) ccmake .\
f)\'a0Set the CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE to Release\
g) Set the CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX to '/opt/odl' or 'C:/Program Files/ODL' if for Windows\
h) Configure and generate\
i) cmake .\
j)\'a0make\
k) sudo make install\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 7) Clone the nImO repository and build it\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sl368\partightenfactor0
\cf2 a) cd ~/git.repositories\
b) git clone https://opendragon@github.com/opendragon/nImO.git\
c) cd nImO/non-iOS\
d) git pull\
e) ccmake .\
f)\'a0Set the CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE to Release\
g) Set the CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX to '/opt/nImO' or 'C:/Program Files/nImO' if for Windows\
h) Configure and generate\
i) cmake .\
j) make\
k) sudo make install\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 l) optional: make test\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 8) nImO uses two configuration files - nimo-config.txt and nimo-services.txt, stored in '/etc/nimo' or 'C:/nImO' for windows. They are in the form of a text representation of a nImO 'map'; nimo-config.txt can be overridden with any of the command-line tools using the '-c' or '\'97config' command-line option.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 a) The file 'nimo-config.txt' has the following keys and they are all optional:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 i)   logger address - the local multicast address to be used for the logger service.\
ii)  logger port - the IP port to be used for the logger service, which must be a non-privileged port.\
iii) registry options - the options to be passed to the registry service on startup.\
iv)  registry path - the path to the registry service; the string '$$' represents the install location for the nImO executables.\
v)   registry search timeout - the time in seconds to wait before determining that the registry service is unavailable.\
vi)  status address - the local multicast address to be used for status messages.\
vii) status port - the IP port to be used for status messages, which must be different from the logger port.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 b) The file 'nimo-services.txt' has keys corresponding to the services that are installed, with values of a map from 'path' to the location of the executable for the service and 'description', a text string that can be displayed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\partightenfactor0
